  <prompt>Generalize the `WorkspacePane` `active-doc-follows-tab` effect (`WorkspacePane.tsx:2283`, today gated `widgetType === 'compose'`) to ALSO fire for `document-viewer` tabs, publishing `{documentId, filename}` (the stable id already on `DocumentViewerWidget.tsx:99-112` widgetData) as the active-item handle. NO new in-widget selection model. Then render per-item CARDS (Summarize · Draft response · Draft memo) keyed to that handle, backed by RAG (lane 2 — `IRagService`/`DocumentSearchHandler`/`DocumentContextService`) + on-demand body: Summarize → chat answer (record-id cited); Draft response/Draft memo → composer/Compose per the widget's interaction pattern. Switching away clears the handle → cards suppress.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React 18 + TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 expertise on the SpaarkeAi WorkspacePane + ConversationPane; comfortable generalizing ONE existing tab-focus effect condition and rendering a reactive per-item card surface without inventing a new selection model.</role>
  <goal>Focusing a document-viewer tab publishes the document as the active-item handle and surfaces three cards with no typing; Summarize answers in chat from RAG/body; switching away clears the handle and suppresses the cards.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-11. The document active item is the FOCUSED `document-viewer` tab's document — published via the tab-focus pattern (FR-04b). Generalize the existing `WorkspacePane` `active-doc-follows-tab` effect (`WorkspacePane.tsx:2283`, today gated `widgetType === 'compose'`) so it ALSO fires for `document-viewer` tabs, publishing `{documentId, filename}` as the active-item handle onto the task-001 conduit. The stable `documentId` already rides on `DocumentViewerWidget`'s `widgetData` (`DocumentViewerWidget.tsx:99-112`) — NO new in-widget selection model is built (that was the RESOLVED unresolved-question). Per-item CARDS Summarize · Draft response · Draft memo render on the ConversationPane proactive-card surface keyed to the handle (reactive, no typing; per ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md per-item→cards). Backing: RAG lane 2 (`IRagService`/`DocumentSearchHandler`/`DocumentContextService`) + on-demand body — content is tool-fetched by id, never a tab snapshot (ADR-015). Landing per interaction pattern (task 022/040 metadata): Summarize → a chat answer with a record-id citation; Draft response / Draft memo → composer/Compose. Switching away from the document-viewer tab clears the handle (single-active-item invariant, task 001) → cards suppress. NFR-07: reactive surface stays distinct from the ADR-047 spine. ConversationPane + WorkspacePane are sequential spines — sequence with 025.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx (active-doc-follows-tab effect :2283, generalize from widgetType === 'compose' to also document-viewer)</file>
