    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse-first / §11: generalize the ONE existing `active-doc-follows-tab` effect condition — build NO new in-widget selection model. Scope: the tab-focus effect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Cards key to the `{documentId, filename}` handle; all content (summary / draft basis) is tool-fetched by id via RAG lane 2 + on-demand body — never a tab/prompt snapshot. Scope: card data.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA">Per-item actions render as CARDS (not chips); no code/tool syntax in labels; collapse the card stack under one disclosure header; hover only on clickable regions. Scope: the card UI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens — cards render correctly in light AND dark mode. Scope: new card UI states.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">Publish the handle via the content-free conduit (task 001), not new content on the PaneEventBus. Scope: the tab-focus publish.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">The card surface is reactive/local — distinct from the ADR-047 server-initiated spine; no new push channel. Scope: the card surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope clause: generalize the effect + render the three cards + wire the RAG-backed actions. Do NOT alter the email cards (task 025); reuse existing RAG/document-context services — no new data path.</constraint>
  </constraints>
