  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor; trace the `active-doc-follows-tab` effect (:2283), the `document-viewer` widgetData `documentId` (:99-112), and the ConversationPane active-item handle consumer.</step>
    <step order="1">Generalize the :2283 effect so it also fires for `document-viewer` tabs, publishing `{documentId, filename}` onto the task-001 conduit (retain the Compose branch; no new selection model).</step>
    <step order="2">Render three cards (Summarize · Draft response · Draft memo) keyed to the handle; appear on focus with NO typing; suppress on tab-switch-away.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire Summarize → RAG lane 2 + on-demand body → a chat answer with a record-id citation.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire Draft response / Draft memo → composer/Compose per the widget's interaction-pattern metadata (022/040).</step>
    <step order="5">Keep the surface distinct from the ADR-047 spine (NFR-07); collapse the card stack under one disclosure header.</step>
    <step order="6">Add unit/interaction tests + ui-tests; verify dark-mode rendering.</step>
    <step order="7">npm run build the Spaarke.AI.Widgets package (if touched) + SpaarkeAi; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Document cards on tab focus"><steps><step>Open a document-viewer tab (focus it); do not type</step></steps><expected>Three cards appear — Summarize · Draft response · Draft memo — keyed to the focused document.</expected></test>
    <test name="Summarize answers in chat from RAG"><steps><step>Focus a document-viewer tab</step><step>Click the Summarize card</step></steps><expected>A summary appears as a chat answer sourced from RAG/on-demand body with a record-id citation — NOT from a tab snapshot.</expected></test>
    <test name="Switch away clears handle"><steps><step>Focus a document-viewer tab (cards appear)</step><step>Switch focus to another tab</step></steps><expected>The active-item handle clears and the three cards suppress.</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark mode"><steps><step>Toggle dark mode; focus a document-viewer tab</step></steps><expected>The three cards use Fluent v9 semantic tokens and are readable in both themes; hover affordances only on clickable regions.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If generalizing the effect requires building a new in-widget selection model or putting document content on the bus/conduit, STOP and escalate (§11 reuse-first / ADR-015) rather than inventing a parallel mechanism. If the card surface would require touching the ADR-047 spine, STOP (NFR-07). Coordinate ConversationPane/WorkspacePane edits with 025 and the analysis-hub/agreements forks (sequential spine).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>The `active-doc-follows-tab` effect (:2283) exists but is gated to Compose; the `document-viewer` widget already exposes a stable `documentId` on widgetData (:99-112); RAG lane 2 services exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — generalize ONE effect condition + render cards over existing RAG services; no new selection model, no new data path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Documents have overview parity but no act-on surface — the second per-item instance is missing; focus a document → no cards → the document per-item DoD fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
