  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Focusing a document-viewer tab publishes `{documentId, filename}` as the active-item handle (via the generalized :2283 effect; no new selection model).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Three cards (Summarize · Draft response · Draft memo) appear on focus with NO typing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Summarize answers in chat from RAG/body with a record-id citation — not from a tab snapshot.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Draft response / Draft memo land on composer/Compose per the widget's interaction-pattern metadata.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Switching away from the document-viewer tab clears the handle and suppresses the cards.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cards render as CARDS (not chips), collapse under one disclosure header, readable in dark mode.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no new in-widget selection model is built; the Compose branch of the effect still works (no regression).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the card surface does NOT touch the ADR-047 spine (NFR-07 preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SpaarkeAi builds; unit/interaction tests pass.</criterion>
